: R5\n        text: \"Implement append mode (-a): when the output file exists, prepend its original content before the stdin content by copying the original file into the temp file first, then appending the stdin buffer. When the output file does not exist, -a behaves as default mode. Per prd007-sponge R3.1-R3.3.\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Implement passthrough mode (no output filename): write the buffered stdin content to stdout after stdin is fully consumed. For large input with temp file spill, seek to beginning and copy to stdout. For small input in memory, write the buffer directly. Per prd007-sponge R4.1-R4.3.\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Exit 0 on success. Exit 1 with a descriptive error message to stderr on any failure (stdin read error, temp file creation/write failure, output file open failure, rename/copy failure, memory allocation failure). Clean up the temp file on all exit paths. Per prd007-sponge R5.1-R5.4.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use the manual flag parsing pattern from cmd/cat/main.go: iterate over os.Args[1:], handle '-a' as append flag, treat '--' as end of flags, remaining positional args are the output filename.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use the SIGPIPE handling pattern from cmd/cat/main.go: create a buffered signal channel, call signal.Notify for SIGPIPE, and exit 0 in a goroutine.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use os.CreateTemp for temp file creation. The directory is os.Getenv('TMPDIR') with fallback to os.TempDir(). The pattern prefix is 'sponge'.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Use os.Rename for atomic write. Detect cross-device failure by checking for *os.LinkError from os.Rename, then fall back to io.Copy from the temp file to a new file at the output path.\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"Use os.Lstat (not os.Stat) to check output path existence and read file mode, per prd007-sponge R2.4. This ensures symlinks are not followed blindly.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/sponge compiles with 'go build ./cmd/sponge/' with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"seq 1 100 | go run ./cmd/sponge /tmp/sponge-test-out.txt creates a file containing lines 1 through 100.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"printf 'hello' | go run ./cmd/sponge writes 'hello' to stdout (passthrough mode).\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Append mode (-a) with an existing file prepends original content before stdin content in the output file.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"An existing output file with mode 0640 retains mode 0640 after sponge overwrites it.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"The temp file does not persist after the process exits, whether due to success or failure.\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"Exit code is 1 and a descriptive message is printed to stderr when the output file path is unwritable.\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"e451caae-fccc-41d8-a534-916f1a5149fa","total_cost_usd":0.79767375,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":107493,"cache_read_input_tokens":18565,"output_tokens":4662,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":107493,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":4662,"cacheReadInputTokens":18565,"cacheCreationInputTokens":107493,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.79767375,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"36e3bd1e-7bf8-479b-a746-4795b6acebfa"}
